      "problem": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n  <td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n    $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n  <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n  \n  <td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n    $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n  <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n  \n  <td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n    $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">\n    {{field-2}}\n  </td>\n  <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n  \n  <td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n    .\n  </td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n  <td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n  <td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n  \n  <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n  \n  <td align=\"center\">\n    $-2$\n  </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
